This project was to convert my old HP Pavilion laptop from Windows 10 to Ubuntu Desktop


Process:
Flashed Ubuntu Desktop to a USB drive
Inserted USB into my laptop
Rebooted and loaded into the boot menu
Choose the USB as the boot drive
Select try or install Ubuntu
Start the installation process through their setup GUI
Laptop has RST protection, and Ubuntu cannot install 
Remove the installation drive and reboot into the BIOS
Disable RST, and remove the Optane drive
Reboot with the installation drive, encounter same error
Troubleshoot for hours on how to bypass RST with no success
Remove the installation drive, and flash it with Ubuntu Server
Reboot laptop with newly flashed drive
Select the USB in the boot menu, select install Ubuntu Server
Go through the installaton process using all default settings
Configure wifi on the wlp1s0 interface, and add device to my home network
Update all packages
Install Ubuntu Desktop from the command line
Reboot system and remove the USB
Voila - Laptop now has Ubuntu Desktop
